## Layer rules (onion)

1. **Domain** (`domain/`) — innermost layer. Entities, repository interfaces
   (ports), domain services. Zero Django/DRF imports. Pure Python.
2. **Application** (`application/`) — use cases and DTOs. Orchestrates
   domain entities via interfaces. No Django/ORM imports (pure Python
   or DRF serializers for DTOs).
3. **Infrastructure** (`infrastructure/`) — outermost layer. Django ORM
   persistence adapters, DRF views/urls. Depends on domain and application.

